window.QUIZ = [{"id": "S26-MC1", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Interrupts", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements about interrupts is <strong>false</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["Interrupts may be generated by hardware devices", "Interrupts may be generated by software exceptions or traps", "All interrupts are serviced in exactly the same way, with no difference in priority", "Interrupts are handled by the kernel"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：interrupt 有 <strong>priority levels</strong>，high-priority 可以 preempt low-priority interrupt <span class=\"sref\">[3.24]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC2", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "DMA", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements is <strong>true</strong> about DMA?</p>\n", "opts": ["DMA is used to move data for slow devices, while CPU is used for fast devices", "DMA allows data transfer between device and memory with less CPU involvement", "DMA eliminates interrupts completely", "CPU and DMA can't execute concurrently"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：DMA 用於 <strong>fast devices / large data</strong>（A 相反）；完成後仍然 <strong>interrupt CPU</strong>（C 錯）；CPU 同 DMA 可以 concurrent（D 錯）<span class=\"sref\">[3.25]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC3", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Storage hierarchy", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements is true about storage hierarchy?</p>\n", "opts": ["Registers are slower than main memory", "Main memory is nonvolatile", "Hard-disk drives are smaller than volatile memory", "Main memory is byte addressable"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>each address refers to one byte</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[1.30]</span>。Registers 最快；main memory volatile；HDD 大過 memory。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC4", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "von Neumann", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is a core characteristic of the von Neumann architecture?</p>\n", "opts": ["Instructions and data are stored in separate physical memories", "Instructions and data are stored in the same memory space, accessed by address", "The CPU does not contain an ALU; all computations are done by an external co-processor", "The Program Counter (PC) is stored in external mass storage devices"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>stored-program architecture</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[1.26]</span>。A 係 Harvard architecture。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC5", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "OS services", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is <strong>false</strong> about services of operating systems?</p>\n", "opts": ["User interface can be CLI or GUI", "The logging service of OS should keep track of computer resources that each user uses", "Errors only occur in memory and I/O devices", "Resource allocation service should allocate resources like CPU cycles, memory, file storage"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：errors 可以喺 <strong>CPU and memory, I/O devices, user programs</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[2.5]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC6", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "API", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is an advantage of using APIs instead of directly invoking system calls?</p>\n", "opts": ["APIs provide a more convenient programming interface", "APIs always execute faster than system calls", "APIs can bypass kernel protection", "APIs eliminate the need for linkers and loaders"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：API 好處 = <strong>portability + hide complex details（convenient）</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[2.17]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC7", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Microkernel", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which is <strong>false</strong> about microkernel system structure?</p>\n", "opts": ["It is easier to extend a microkernel operating system", "It typically has better performance than a monolithic kernel", "It runs memory management in user space", "It is easier to port a microkernel operating system to new architectures"], "ans": "B", "alt": "C", "exp": "<p>解：microkernel <strong>performance suffers</strong>（message passing overhead）<span class=\"sref\">[2.48]</span>；microkernel 保留 minimal memory management 喺 kernel，所以 C 都算錯。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC8", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "printf vs write", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>What's the relationship between printf() and write()?</p>\n", "opts": ["Both printf() and write() are system calls provided directly by the kernel", "printf() invokes write() system call to get service from operating system", "The program enters kernel mode immediately when printf() is called", "write() system call invokes printf() to perform the print function"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>printf() 係 C library function，佢 call write() system call</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[2.26]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC9", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Layered design", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements about a layered operating-system design is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["Any layer may directly access any other layer", "The interfaces between adjacent layers are usually well defined", "Layered design eliminates all performance overhead", "Pure layered design is the dominant structure in all modern operating systems"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：每層只用下層服務、interface well defined（information hiding）<span class=\"sref\">[2.44–2.45]</span>。A 係 LKM 特色；layered 有 overhead；好少 pure layered。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC10", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork count", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"c\"><code>int main() {\n   int i;\n   for (i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {\n      if (fork() == 0) {\n         fork();\n         printf(&quot;X &quot;);\n         return 1;\n      }\n   }\n   printf(&quot;Y &quot;);\n   return 0;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>What is the total number of processes (including the original), the number of &quot;X &quot; printed, and the number of &quot;Y &quot; printed?</p>\n", "opts": ["Total processes = 4, &quot;X &quot; = 3, &quot;Y &quot; = 1", "Total processes = 4, &quot;X &quot; = 1, &quot;Y &quot; = 3", "Total processes = 7, &quot;X &quot; = 6, &quot;Y &quot; = 1", "Total processes = 7, &quot;X &quot; = 1, &quot;Y &quot; = 6"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：只有 original 繼續 loop；每輪生 1 個 child，child 再 fork → 2 個印 X 然後 return。3 輪 × 2 = <strong>6 X</strong>；original 印 <strong>1 Y</strong>；total = 1 + 6 = <strong>7</strong>（已用 C 程式驗證）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC11", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Context switch", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement is true about context switch?</p>\n", "opts": ["Context switch means switching from user mode to kernel mode", "During context switch, OS saves the state of one process/thread and restores another", "Context switch requires the same hardware on all CPU architectures", "Context switch is shorter if the OS is more complex"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.20]</span>。A 係 mode switch；越複雜 OS/PCB → context switch <strong>越長</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC12", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Ordinary pipes", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement about ordinary pipes is <strong>false</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["They can be accessed like file descriptors", "They can be accessed by arbitrary processes", "They disappear after the communicating processes terminate", "They are typically used between parent and child processes"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>ordinary pipe cannot be accessed from outside the process that creates it</strong>（只限 parent–child）<span class=\"sref\">[3.65–3.66]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC13", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Zombie", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement about zombie processes is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["A zombie process is still executing user code normally", "A zombie process has terminated but its parent has not yet collected its status", "A zombie process is created when exec() fails", "A zombie process owns no process identifier"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.49]</span> terminated 但 parent 未 call wait()；<strong>PID、process-table entry、PCB 仍然存在</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC14", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Leaving running state", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which event typically causes a process to leave the running state?</p>\n", "opts": ["It issues an I/O request", "It calls a function", "It increases a local variable", "It reads from cache"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：I/O request → running → <strong>waiting</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[3.9]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC15", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Multithreaded process", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is true about the multithreaded process?</p>\n", "opts": ["Each thread has its own address space and file descriptors", "Threads can't run concurrently on multiple cores if they belong to the same process", "Thread creation is usually faster than process creation", "It can't take advantage of processing capabilities on multicore systems"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>Economy</strong> — thread creation cheaper <span class=\"sref\">[4.4, 4.7]</span>；threads share address space &amp; files。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC16", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Concurrency vs parallelism", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement is correct about concurrency and parallelism in multicore systems?</p>\n", "opts": ["Concurrency means a system can perform more than one task at exactly the same time", "Parallelism means tasks only make progress over time on a single processor core", "Concurrency can be supported on a single processor core through time multiplexing by the scheduler", "Testing and debugging become easier in multicore systems because execution paths are fixed"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.9]</span>。A 係 parallelism 定義；debugging 變<strong>難</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC17", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Amdahl's Law", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which combination gives a speedup between 1.6 and 1.7?</p>\n", "opts": ["parallel 81%, 3 cores", "parallel 81%, 5 cores", "parallel 61%, 3 cores", "parallel 61%, 5 cores"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">speedup</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.3651em;vertical-align:-0.52em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.52em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>。A：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2484em;vertical-align:-0.4033em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.19</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.27</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4033em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.17</span></span></span></span>；B：2.84；<strong>C：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.2484em;vertical-align:-0.4033em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.39</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.2033</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.4033em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.69</span></span></span></span></strong>；D：1.95。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC18", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Signals", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement about signal handling is <strong>false</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["Signals can be received synchronously or asynchronously", "Users can define custom signal handlers for certain signals", "All signals should be delivered to all threads in a process", "Different signals can have different handlers in the same process"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：synchronous signals 只 deliver 畀 <strong>causing thread</strong>；只有部分 asynchronous（e.g. Ctrl-C terminate）先畀所有 threads <span class=\"sref\">[4.30–4.31]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC19", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Scheduling criteria", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement about scheduling criteria is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["Waiting time is the amount of time from process arrival until the process finishes execution", "Turnaround time is the amount of time a process spends waiting in the ready queue", "Response time is the amount of time from when a request is submitted until the first response is produced", "Throughput is the fraction of time the CPU is busy"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：A 係 turnaround；B 係 waiting；D 係 CPU utilization <span class=\"sref\">[5.8, 5.12]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC20", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "MLFQ", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement about MLFQ is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["Processes never move between queues", "Each queue can use a different scheduling algorithm", "It requires burst times to be known exactly in advance", "It is a non-preemptive algorithm"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.30–5.31]</span>。MLFQ 可以搬 queue、唔需要知 burst、preemptive。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC21", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "EDF", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which scheduling algorithm assigns priorities according to deadlines?</p>\n", "opts": ["RM", "EDF", "FCFS", "RR"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：EDF = dynamic priority by deadline；RM = static by period <span class=\"sref\">[5.51]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC22", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Multiprocessor scheduling", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which statement about multiprocessor scheduling is <strong>false</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["For asymmetric multiprocessing, the master server can become a potential bottleneck", "In a multithreaded system, another thread may run when one thread stalls while waiting for memory", "The motivation of placing multiple processor cores on the same physical chip is to simplify the scheduler", "Processor affinity tries to keep a process on the same CPU to improve cache performance"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：multicore 係為咗 <strong>faster + less power</strong>，而且令 scheduling <strong>更複雜</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[5.40]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC23", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Mutex + semaphore output", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"c\"><code>int counter = 0; pthread_mutex_t mtx; sem_t sem;   /* sem_init(&amp;sem, 0, 0) */\nvoid *worker1(void *arg) { pthread_mutex_lock(&amp;mtx); counter = counter + 2;\n    printf(&quot;A %d;&quot;, counter); pthread_mutex_unlock(&amp;mtx); sem_post(&amp;sem); return NULL; }\nvoid *worker2(void *arg) { sem_wait(&amp;sem); pthread_mutex_lock(&amp;mtx); counter = counter + 3;\n    printf(&quot;B %d;&quot;, counter); pthread_mutex_unlock(&amp;mtx); return NULL; }\n/* main creates t1 (worker1) and t2 (worker2), then joins both */\n</code></pre>\n<p>What is the output?</p>\n", "opts": ["A 2; B 5;", "B 3; A 5;", "A 3; B 5;", "B 2; A 4;"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：sem 初始 0 → worker2 一定等 worker1 <code>sem_post</code> → 先 A（0+2=2）後 B（2+3=5）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC24", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Hardware primitive", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>Which hardware primitive is commonly used to build synchronization tools?</p>\n", "opts": ["exec()", "test_and_set()", "fork()", "open()"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：atomic hardware instructions：<strong>test_and_set()、compare_and_swap()</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[6.14]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "S26-MC25", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Bounded-waiting TAS", "kind": "past", "src": "S26", "stem": "<p>In the bounded-waiting mutual exclusion algorithm using test_and_set() (waiting[], key, lock; exit section scans j = (i+1)%n … and either sets lock = false or waiting[j] = false), which statement is <strong>not correct</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["test_and_set(&amp;lock) releases the lock after the critical section", "waiting[i] is used to indicate that process i wants to enter the critical section", "waiting[j] = false indicates that process i releases the lock (hands it to j)", "Process i can re-enter the critical section after executing lock = false"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：test_and_set 只會 <strong>set lock = true（acquire）</strong>；release 係 <code>lock = false</code> 或者 <code>waiting[j] = false</code> <span class=\"sref\">[6.19]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC1", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Locality", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Locality is essential to ____</p>\n", "opts": ["Memory", "Cache", "Hard disks", "Non-volatile memory (NVM)"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：caching works because of <strong>temporal/spatial locality</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[1.33]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC2", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Virtualization", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>____ allows a guest OS to run as an application on a native OS.</p>\n", "opts": ["Operating system", "Emulation", "User interface", "Virtualization"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.43]</span> &quot;allows an OS to run as an application within another OS&quot;。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC3", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Interrupt", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements about interrupts is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["Interrupts enable hardware to interact with the operating system", "Interrupt alerts the CPU that some event requires attention", "Interrupt allows software to access hardware including the CPU", "Interrupt can be caused by both hardware and software"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：C 講緊 <strong>system call</strong> 嘅功能。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC4", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "API", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Programmers interface with ____ to obtain services from the OS.</p>\n", "opts": ["Shell", "System call interfaces", "APIs (application programming interfaces)", "System calls"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：programmers 用 <strong>API</strong>（best answer）<span class=\"sref\">[2.15]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC5", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Parameter passing", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>How can parameters be passed to the OS in system calls?</p>\n", "opts": ["Registers", "Stack", "Block or table", "All of the above"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：三種方法 <span class=\"sref\">[2.20]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC6", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "LKM", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>____ refers to the OS design that maintains a set of core components in the kernel and adds additional services via modules during run time.</p>\n", "opts": ["Layered approach", "Loadable kernel modules (LKMs)", "Microkernel", "Monolithic"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.49]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC7", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements on fork() is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["The parent process waits until the completion of the child process", "The child process duplicates the entire address space of the parent process", "The parent and child processes run the same program", "The parent and child processes run concurrently in the system"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：等 child 係 <strong>wait()</strong> 嘅工作，fork 本身唔會等。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC8", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Address space", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is contained in the address space of a process?</p>\n", "opts": ["Stack", "Code", "Data", "All of the above"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：text (code)、data、heap、stack <span class=\"sref\">[3.5]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC9", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Named pipes", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>____ enables communication for multiple processes with no parent-child relationship, independent from network.</p>\n", "opts": ["RPCs", "Ordinary pipes", "Named pipes", "Socket"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：named pipes 唔需要 parent-child、多 processes 用 <span class=\"sref\">[3.69]</span>；socket/RPC 要 network。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC10", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Medium-term scheduler", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>____ swaps a process out of memory and temporarily stores it on disk.</p>\n", "opts": ["The long-term scheduler", "A device scheduler", "The CPU scheduler", "The medium-term scheduler"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>swapping</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[3.18]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC11", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Not shared by threads", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Which item below is <strong>NOT</strong> shared by threads of the same process?</p>\n", "opts": ["Code", "Stack", "Files", "Data"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：每個 thread 有自己 <strong>stack, registers, PC</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[4.6]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC12", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Thread library", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>____ provides the programmer with an API for creating and managing threads.</p>\n", "opts": ["Thread library (such as POSIX Pthreads)", "Signals", "System calls", "Inter-process communications"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.20]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC13", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Multithreading models", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["Kernel threads are scheduled by the OS", "Programmers or users manage user threads", "A user thread can be mapped to more than one kernel thread", "One user thread can be mapped to at most one kernel thread"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：冇 one-to-many mapping；many-to-many 係 many user → <strong>smaller or equal</strong> kernel threads。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC14", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Minimum average waiting time", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Given a set of processes, which algorithm produces the minimum average waiting time?</p>\n", "opts": ["FCFS", "RR", "SJF", "SRTF"], "ans": "C", "alt": "D", "exp": "<p>解：SJF optimal among non-preemptive；SRTF optimal among preemptive <span class=\"sref\">[5.17, 5.24]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "F20-MC15", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Hard to implement", "kind": "past", "src": "F20", "stem": "<p>Which of the following scheduling algorithms is difficult to implement in practice?</p>\n", "opts": ["SJF", "RR", "MLFQ", "FCFS"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：好難知道 <strong>next CPU burst length</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[5.17]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC1", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "von Neumann", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>In a von Neumann architecture, a processing unit contains a/an ____ and processor registers.</p>\n", "opts": ["arithmetic logic unit (ALU)", "instruction register (IR)", "program counter (PC)", "all of the mentioned"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.26]</span> &quot;a CPU that contains an ALU and processor registers&quot;；IR 屬 control unit。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC2", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Interrupt trigger", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following events will directly trigger an interrupt?</p>\n", "opts": ["kernel code execution", "I/O job execution", "user code execution", "I/O job completion"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：device controller 完成操作 → <strong>interrupt</strong> CPU <span class=\"sref\">[3.21]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC3", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Dual mode", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>The two separate modes of operation in an operating system are ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["supervisor mode and system mode", "physical mode and logical mode", "user mode and kernel mode", "kernel mode and privileged mode"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.27]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC4", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "System calls", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>____ provide an interface to the services provided by an operating system.</p>\n", "opts": ["Inter-process communications", "Remote procedure calls", "System calls", "User interfaces"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.14]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC5", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Original UNIX", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which operating system structure is adopted by the original UNIX?</p>\n", "opts": ["layered structure", "microkernel", "monolithic structure", "modular approach"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.40–2.41]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC6", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Degree of multiprogramming", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>The ____ refers to the number of processes in the memory.</p>\n", "opts": ["program counter", "degree of multi-programming", "long-term scheduler", "CPU scheduler"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.14]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC7", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Amdahl", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Using Amdahl's Law, what is the speedup for an application that is 30% serial on 7 processing cores?</p>\n", "opts": ["2", "2.5", "3", "3.5"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.3651em;vertical-align:-0.52em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.3</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.7/7</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.52em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1901em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0.4</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span></span></span> <strong>2.5</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC8", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Process owns", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>In an operating system, each process has its own ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["address space", "local/global variables and open files", "pending alarms, signals and signal handlers", "all of the above"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：process = address space + resources。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC9", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Stack", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which section of a process contains temporary data like function parameters, return addresses and local variables?</p>\n", "opts": ["text section", "data section", "heap", "stack"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.5]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC10", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Short-term scheduler", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following selects from among the processes in the ready queue to execute on the CPU?</p>\n", "opts": ["Short-term scheduler", "Medium-term scheduler", "Long-term scheduler", "Context switcher"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：= CPU scheduler <span class=\"sref\">[3.17]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC11", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork incorrect", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>During process creation with fork(), which of the following is <strong>incorrect</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["The child process can run concurrently with the parent", "The child process can call wait() in order to finish earlier than the parent", "The child process can call exec() to load a new program into it", "The child can be an exact duplicate of the parent"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：wait() 係等 <strong>child</strong> 完成，唔係令自己早完。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC12", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Pipes", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following statements about pipes is <strong>not</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["Named pipes allow bi-directional communication", "Only the parent and child processes can use ordinary pipes for communication", "Named pipes cease to exist after the communicating processes have finished", "Reading and writing to ordinary pipes on both UNIX and Windows can be performed like ordinary file I/O"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：named pipes <strong>continue to exist until explicitly deleted</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[3.69]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC13", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Leave the CPU", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following events might force a process to leave the CPU?</p>\n", "opts": ["make a fork system call", "make an I/O request", "interrupt", "all of the above"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：system call / I/O / interrupt 都可以令 process 離開 CPU。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC14", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork with ||", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"c\"><code>if (fork() || fork()) {\n   fork();\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>How many processes are created in total (including the original)?</p>\n", "opts": ["3", "4", "5", "6"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：P0（true，跳過第二個 fork）→ fork → 2；C1（false）→ fork2：C1 true → fork → 2；C2 false → 1。<strong>2 + 2 + 1 = 5</strong> <span class=\"ok\">✅</span></p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC15", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork in loop", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"c\"><code>for (int i = 0; i &lt; 3; ++i) {\n   if (fork() == 0) fork();\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>How many processes in total?</p>\n", "opts": ["3", "8", "27", "64"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：每輪每個 process 變 3 個 → <strong><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">27</span></span></span></span></strong> <span class=\"ok\">✅</span></p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC16", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "TCB", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is <strong>not</strong> in the Thread Control Block (TCB)?</p>\n", "opts": ["Execution state", "Scheduling information", "Pointer to enclosing process", "Process identifier"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：TCB 有 execution state、scheduling info、accounting、pointers、<strong>pointer to enclosing PCB</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[4.15]</span>；PID 喺 PCB。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC17", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Concurrency", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which refers to the capability to allow multiple tasks to make progress on a single processor?</p>\n", "opts": ["parallelism", "concurrency", "data parallelism", "task parallelism"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.9]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC18", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Multithreading models", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following is <strong>not</strong> true about multithreading models?</p>\n", "opts": ["Many-to-one means many user-level threads are mapped to a single kernel thread", "One-to-one model provides more concurrency than many-to-one model", "The many-to-many model is easy to implement in practice", "Most operating systems now use the one-to-one model"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：many-to-many <strong>difficult to implement</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[4.26]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC19", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Thread-local storage", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Thread-local storage is data that ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["is not associated with any process", "has been modified by the thread, but not yet updated to the parent process", "is generated by the thread independent of the thread's process", "is unique to each thread"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：TLS = <strong>unique to each thread</strong>（Windows TEB 入面有 TLS <span class=\"sref\">[4.36]</span>）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC20", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "When scheduling occurs", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>CPU scheduling decisions may take place when ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["a process switches from running to waiting state", "a process terminates", "a process switches from running to ready state", "all of the above"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：四種情況 <span class=\"sref\">[5.6]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC21", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Priority problem", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>The main problem with a priority scheduling algorithm is ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["how to set the priority of a process", "some processes may never execute", "how to determine the length of the next CPU burst", "how to determine the length of the time quantum"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<strong>starvation</strong>；solution = aging <span class=\"sref\">[5.25]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC22", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "RR large quantum", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>For RR scheduling, when the time quantum q gets too large, it degenerates to ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["SJF", "FCFS", "Shortest-remaining-time-first", "Multilevel queue"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.14, 5.16]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC23", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Must be non-preemptive", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which of the following scheduling algorithms must be non-preemptive?</p>\n", "opts": ["FCFS", "SJF", "Priority scheduling", "Multi-level feedback queue"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：FCFS 一定 non-preemptive；SJF / priority 有 preemptive 版本；MLFQ preemptive <span class=\"sref\">[5.11]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC24", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "MLFQ true statement", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>In the multilevel feedback queue algorithm, which statement is true?</p>\n", "opts": ["Prior knowledge on the next CPU burst time is required for scheduling", "Classification of the ready queue is permanent", "It handles interactive jobs well by delivering similar performance as SJF", "It won't suffer from starvation problem"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.35]</span>。B 係 multilevel queue（冇 feedback）；MLFQ 都可能 starvation（要 reshuffle/aging）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC25", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Real-time", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which statement about real-time CPU scheduling is true?</p>\n", "opts": ["Real-time scheduling doesn't demand performance guarantee", "In hard real-time systems, a task can be serviced after its deadline", "Soft real-time systems guarantee only that the process will be prioritized over non-critical processes", "The scheduler for a real-time system must support a priority-based algorithm without preemption"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.47]</span>。RT scheduler 要 <strong>priority-based with preemption</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC26", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Starvation-free", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Which algorithms are free from starvation? 1. FCFS 2. Non-preemptive SJF 3. Preemptive SJF 4. Round Robin 5. Multi-level Queue</p>\n", "opts": ["1 4", "1 2 4", "1 3 4", "1 2 4 5"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：SJF/SRTF 長 job 可能 starve；multilevel queue（fixed priority）低 queue 可能 starve；<strong>FCFS、RR 唔會</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC27", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Mutual exclusion", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Mutual exclusion implies that ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["if a process is executing in its critical section, then no other process can be executing in their critical sections", "if a process is executing in its critical section, then only one of the other processes can be executing in its critical section", "if a process is executing in its critical section, then all the resources of the system must be blocked until it finishes execution", "none of the above"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.11]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC28", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "CS requirements", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>A solution to the critical section problem does <strong>not</strong> have to satisfy which requirement?</p>\n", "opts": ["mutual exclusion", "progress", "synchronization", "bounded waiting"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：三個 requirements = ME + progress + bounded waiting。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC29", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Race condition", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>A situation where several processes access and manipulate the same data concurrently and the outcome depends on the particular order of access is called ____.</p>\n", "opts": ["data consistency", "race condition", "aging", "starvation"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.9]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Sp21-MC30", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Entry section", "kind": "past", "src": "Sp21", "stem": "<p>Suppose the binary variable lock is initialized to 0. Which can be an implementation of the entry section to solve the critical-section problem?</p>\n", "opts": ["while (compare_and_swap(&amp;lock, 0, 1) == 0) ;", "while (compare_and_swap(&amp;lock, 1, 0) != 0) ;", "while (test_and_set(&amp;lock)) ;", "while (!test_and_set(&amp;lock)) ;"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：TAS 返回 old value；lock = 0 時第一個 process 得 0 → 跳出 loop 入 CS <span class=\"sref\">[6.16]</span>。A 嘅條件相反（應該 <code>!= 0</code>）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC1", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "DMA", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about I/O operations and DMA is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["In programmed I/O, the CPU executes special I/O instructions to move data between a device controller and memory", "A DMA controller can transfer a block of data between an I/O device and memory without continuous CPU involvement", "During a DMA transfer, the DMA controller sends an interrupt to the CPU after every byte is transferred", "After a DMA block transfer completes, the DMA controller can interrupt the CPU"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：DMA <strong>block 完成先 interrupt 一次</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[3.25–3.26]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC2", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Interrupts and traps", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about interrupts and traps is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["Hardware interrupts are generally asynchronous to the instruction currently being executed", "Interrupts can only be generated by I/O devices", "A trap or exception may be caused by an error or by a user request such as a system call", "Interrupts may have different priority levels"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：trap/exception = <strong>software-generated interrupt</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[3.24]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC3", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Resource allocator", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Several jobs are ready to run on a shared computer. The OS decides which job receives CPU time and how memory is allocated. Which role does this illustrate?</p>\n", "opts": ["The OS provides a user interface", "The OS provides a communication service", "The OS acts as a resource allocator", "The OS acts as an application program"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.23]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC4", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "NUMA", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about multiprocessor, multicore, and NUMA systems is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["In SMP, processors have their own registers and local caches but share physical memory", "A multicore system places multiple computing cores on a single physical chip", "In NUMA, a CPU can access its local memory faster than remote memory connected to another CPU group", "In NUMA, every CPU accesses every part of memory with exactly the same latency"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：NUMA = <strong>non-uniform</strong> latency <span class=\"sref\">[1.40]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC5", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "OS structures", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about operating-system structures is <strong>true</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["A monolithic kernel moves most OS services into user-space processes that communicate by message passing", "A microkernel keeps only essential functions in the kernel and provides other services outside the kernel through communication mechanisms such as message passing", "In a layered OS, each layer may directly call any other layer without restriction", "A loadable kernel module always requires the entire kernel to be recompiled and the machine to be rebooted"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.46–2.47]</span>。A 描述 microkernel 唔係 monolithic；C 錯；LKM 唔使 recompile/reboot。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC6", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "read() path", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>A C program calls read() to obtain data from a file. Which sequence best describes how the request reaches the OS?</p>\n", "opts": ["The application directly executes the device's privileged I/O instructions while remaining in user mode", "The read() API completes the entire file operation in user mode without invoking the kernel", "The API and run-time environment use the system-call interface to invoke the corresponding kernel service, and control later returns to the application", "The OS creates a new process to execute every read() request"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.18–2.19]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC7", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Privileged instruction", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>What normally happens if a user program attempts to execute a privileged instruction in user mode?</p>\n", "opts": ["The hardware treats the instruction as illegal and traps to the operating system", "The CPU automatically changes the instruction into a non-privileged instruction", "The user program changes the mode bit by itself and continues in kernel mode", "The instruction is always executed, but its result is discarded"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.28]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC8", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Virtualization", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about virtualization is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["A virtual machine manager creates and manages virtual machines", "An application always runs faster inside a virtual machine than directly on the physical machine", "Each guest OS runs in its own VM and behaves as if it has access to hardware", "Virtualization allows multiple operating systems to run on one physical machine"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：VM 只會 <strong>minor performance decrease</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[1.46]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC9", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about fork() is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["After a successful fork(), the child receives 0 and the parent receives the child's PID", "The parent and child both continue execution at the instruction following fork()", "If the child changes a global variable after fork(), the parent's copy changes automatically", "The execution order of parent and child depends on scheduling unless synchronization is used"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：各自有 <strong>own copy</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW1-MC10", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Pipes", "kind": "past", "src": "HW1", "stem": "<p>Which statement about pipes is <strong>NOT</strong> true?</p>\n", "opts": ["An ordinary pipe is typically used between processes with a parent-child relationship", "A named pipe can be used by processes that do not have a parent-child relationship", "An ordinary pipe is typically unidirectional", "A named pipe ceases to exist as soon as the communicating processes terminate"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：named pipe 要 <strong>explicitly deleted</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC1", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Responsiveness", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>An interactive application continues responding to the user while one of its threads is blocked. Which benefit does this illustrate?</p>\n", "opts": ["Economy", "Responsiveness", "Resource sharing", "Scalability"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.7]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC2", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Data parallelism", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>Which arrangement is an example of data parallelism?</p>\n", "opts": ["Threads on different cores each perform a different operation", "One thread processes all elements of an array sequentially", "One thread handles user input while another thread performs spelling checks", "Threads on different cores perform the same operation on different subsets of an array"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：A、C = task parallelism；B = serial <span class=\"sref\">[4.11]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC3", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Signal classification", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>Which statement correctly classifies signals?</p>\n", "opts": ["Division by zero can generate a synchronous signal, whereas timer expiration can generate an asynchronous signal", "Division by zero can generate an asynchronous signal, whereas timer expiration can generate a synchronous signal", "Both generate synchronous signals", "Both generate asynchronous signals"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.29]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC4", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Deferred cancellation", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>Which statement describes deferred thread cancellation?</p>\n", "opts": ["The target thread is terminated immediately when cancellation is requested", "Requesting cancellation terminates every thread in its process", "The target thread periodically checks whether it should terminate, allowing it to terminate in an orderly manner", "The target thread can be canceled only after it has finished its normal execution"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：A 係 asynchronous cancellation <span class=\"sref\">[4.32]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC5", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Preemptive scheduling", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>Which event is an example of preemptive CPU scheduling?</p>\n", "opts": ["A running process completes its execution and terminates", "A running process requests I/O and enters the waiting state", "A time quantum expires, and the running process is moved back to the ready queue", "A running process calls wait() and enters the waiting state"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：running → ready（involuntary）= preemptive <span class=\"sref\">[5.6]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC6", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Convoy effect", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>Which situation illustrates the convoy effect in FCFS?</p>\n", "opts": ["A waiting process gradually gains a higher priority", "Several short processes wait behind a long process that arrived first", "A process moves to a lower-priority queue after using its time quantum", "A running process is preempted when its RR quantum expires"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.10]</span>。A = aging；C = MLFQ demotion。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC7", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Aging", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>What is the purpose of aging in priority scheduling?</p>\n", "opts": ["To address starvation by gradually increasing the priority of a waiting process", "To keep each process permanently in the same priority queue", "To predict the length of a process's next CPU burst", "To give higher priority to periodic tasks with shorter periods"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.25]</span>。D = RM。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC8", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "PCS vs SCS", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>In a many-to-many model, a thread library selects a user thread to run on an available LWP. Which scheduling scope applies?</p>\n", "opts": ["SCS, because several user threads are competing", "SCS, because the library schedules kernel threads onto CPUs", "PCS, because all kernel threads in the system are competing", "PCS, because the competing threads belong to the same process"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.37]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC9", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Exponential averaging", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>The predicted CPU burst is 10 ms, the actual burst is 6 ms, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.25</span></span></span></span>. What is the next prediction?</p>\n", "opts": ["6 ms", "7 ms", "9 ms", "10 ms"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6389em;vertical-align:-0.2083em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.25</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.75</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span></span></span> <strong>9</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "HW2-MC10", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Little's formula", "kind": "past", "src": "HW2", "stem": "<p>3 processes arrive per second on average; average queue length is 12. Average waiting time?</p>\n", "opts": ["0.25 s", "4 s", "9 s", "36 s"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">W</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">12/3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span></span></span> <strong>4 s</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[5.57]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "Lab4-MC", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Threads share memory, processes do not", "kind": "past", "src": "Lab4", "stem": "<pre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"c\"><code>void *child(void *arg) { int *counter = (int *) arg; (*counter)++; return NULL; }\nint main() {\n    int counter = 0;  pthread_t thread;\n    pthread_create(&amp;thread, NULL, child, (void *)&amp;counter);\n    pthread_join(thread, NULL);\n    printf(&quot;%d\\n&quot;, counter);\n    counter = 0;\n    pid_t pid = fork();\n    if (pid) wait(NULL);\n    else { child((void *)&amp;counter); exit(0); }\n    printf(&quot;%d\\n&quot;, counter);\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>What is the output?</p>\n", "opts": ["0 then 0", "1 then 0", "0 then 1", "1 then 1"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：thread 同 main 共用 <code>counter</code> → 印 1；fork 出嚟嘅 child 改嘅係自己嗰份 copy → parent 印 0。<strong>Threads share memory space, processes have separate memory spaces.</strong>（Lab 4）</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-1", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Storage managed by", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>According to the storage characteristics table, which level of storage is managed by the <strong>compiler</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["Registers", "Cache", "Main memory", "Solid-state disk"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：registers – compiler；cache – hardware；main memory / SSD / disk – OS <span class=\"sref\">[1.34]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-2", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Bootstrap", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Where is the bootstrap program (the first program run at power-on) typically stored?</p>\n", "opts": ["DRAM", "Cache", "EEPROM", "Hard disk"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.30]</span> bootstrap program stored on EEPROM（firmware）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-3", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Multiprocessor speedup", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Why is the speed-up ratio with N processors less than N?</p>\n", "opts": ["Each processor runs a different instruction set", "Overhead, e.g., contention for shared resources such as the bus or memory", "Only one processor can execute user processes", "Processors must share a single register set"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.37]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-4", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Multiprocessor advantages", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which is <strong>NOT</strong> an advantage of multiprocessor systems listed in the lecture?</p>\n", "opts": ["Increased throughput", "Economy of scale", "Increased reliability (graceful degradation)", "Simpler parallel programming"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：multiprocessor 令 parallel programming <strong>更複雜</strong> [1.37, summary]。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-5", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "NUMA drawback", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>What is the potential drawback of a NUMA system?</p>\n", "opts": ["All CPUs must share a single slow bus", "Increased latency when a CPU must access remote memory across the system interconnect", "CPUs cannot share one physical address space", "It consumes more power than multicore chips"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.40]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-6", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Cloud models", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A database server provided as a ready-to-use software stack over the Internet is an example of:</p>\n", "opts": ["SaaS", "PaaS", "IaaS", "MaaS"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：SaaS = applications；<strong>PaaS = software stack (e.g. database server)</strong>；IaaS = servers/storage <span class=\"sref\">[1.48]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-7", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "VMM", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about virtualization components is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["The guest OS creates and manages the virtual machine manager", "The VMM (hypervisor) creates and manages VMs, providing an interface identical to the host", "The host is the virtual copy given to each guest", "Programs in a VM usually run several times faster than natively"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.44]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-8", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Timesharing", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["Multiprogramming is an extension of timesharing", "Timesharing switches jobs so frequently that users can interact with each job while it runs", "Timesharing requires that only one program be in memory", "Multiprogramming is not used in modern systems"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：timesharing = logical extension of multiprogramming <span class=\"sref\">[1.42]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-9", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "Mechanical vs electrical storage", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Compared with mechanical storage (e.g., HDD), electrical storage (NVM) is generally:</p>\n", "opts": ["Larger and cheaper per byte", "More costly, smaller, more reliable and faster", "Slower but more reliable", "Volatile"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[1.31]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch1-10", "ch": "ch1", "topic": "AMAT", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A cache has hit ratio 95%, hit time 1 ns and miss time 100 ns. The average access time is:</p>\n", "opts": ["1.0 ns", "5.0 ns", "5.95 ns", "100 ns"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.95</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.95</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span></span></span> <strong>5.95 ns</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-1", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "ioctl", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In UNIX, <code>ioctl()</code> belongs to which category of system calls?</p>\n", "opts": ["Process control", "File management", "Device management", "Protection"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.25]</span> device management：ioctl()、read()、write()。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-2", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "chmod", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p><code>chmod()</code>, <code>umask()</code> and <code>chown()</code> are examples of which category of system calls?</p>\n", "opts": ["Information maintenance", "Communications", "Protection", "File management"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.25]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-3", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Parameter passing limit", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which parameter-passing methods do <strong>not</strong> limit the number or length of parameters?</p>\n", "opts": ["Registers only", "Block (table) and stack methods", "Registers and stack", "None of them"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.20]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-4", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Policy vs mechanism", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Deciding how long the timer should be set for a particular user is an example of:</p>\n", "opts": ["A mechanism", "A policy", "A system call", "A system program"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：timer 本身 = mechanism；設幾耐 = policy <span class=\"sref\">[2.34]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-5", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Shell", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>What is the primary functionality of a shell?</p>\n", "opts": ["Schedule kernel threads", "Fetch a command from the user, interpret it and execute it", "Manage virtual memory", "Load device drivers"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.8]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-6", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "DLL", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>What is a benefit of dynamically linked libraries (DLLs)?</p>\n", "opts": ["They are linked statically into every executable", "They are loaded when needed and shared by all programs using the same version", "They remove the need for a loader", "They make executables larger"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.31]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-7", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "MS-DOS", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about MS-DOS is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["It is a multitasking system with dual mode", "Application programs could access I/O directly, and it had no dual mode or hardware protection", "It is a microkernel design", "It creates a new process for every program"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.36, 2.39]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-8", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Microkernel services", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A microkernel typically provides:</p>\n", "opts": ["File systems and device drivers only", "Minimal process and memory management, plus a communication facility", "The GUI and shells", "All OS services in kernel mode"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.46]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-9", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Darwin", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Darwin, the kernel environment of macOS/iOS, consists of:</p>\n", "opts": ["Linux kernel and glibc", "Mach microkernel and BSD UNIX kernel", "Windows NT kernel and personalities", "ART and JNI"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.54, 2.57]</span>（hybrid，XNU kernel）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-10", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Android", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about Android is <strong>false</strong>?</p>\n", "opts": ["Java applications execute on the Android RunTime (ART)", "Programs written using JNI are generally portable across hardware", "Android uses the Bionic C library instead of glibc", "The HAL abstracts hardware to provide a consistent view"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：JNI programs <strong>generally not portable</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[2.58]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-11", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "Windows structure", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Windows is described as:</p>\n", "opts": ["Pure microkernel", "Largely monolithic with microkernel-like subsystems (personalities) and loadable modules", "Pure layered", "Simple structure like MS-DOS"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.52]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch2-12", "ch": "ch2", "topic": "High-level language", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which is a main advantage of implementing an OS in a high-level language?</p>\n", "opts": ["Always faster than assembly", "Easier to port to other hardware", "Less storage needed", "No compiler needed"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[2.35]</span>；缺點 = reduced speed、more storage。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-1", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Default file descriptors", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>On UNIX, each process by default has three open file descriptors. Which are they?</p>\n", "opts": ["stdin (0), stdout (1), stderr (2)", "stdin (1), stdout (2), stderr (3)", "pipe read end, pipe write end, stderr", "stdin, stdout, swap"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.7]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-2", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Linux PCB", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In Linux, the PCB is represented by:</p>\n", "opts": ["struct pcb in a hash table", "struct task_struct elements in a circular doubly linked list (task list)", "TCB in a binary tree", "ETHREAD"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.13]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-3", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Long-term scheduler", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about the long-term scheduler is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["It is invoked every few milliseconds", "It controls the degree of multiprogramming and is mainly used in mainframes, not PCs", "It swaps processes out to disk", "It selects the next process from the ready queue"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.17]</span>。C = medium-term；D = short-term。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-4", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Register sets", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Some processors (e.g., SUN UltraSPARC) provide multiple register sets. What is the effect on context switch?</p>\n", "opts": ["Context switch becomes impossible", "A context switch may just change the pointer to a different register set", "The PCB is no longer needed", "Context switch time increases"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.20]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-5", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Copy-on-write", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In Linux, fork() uses copy-on-write. What does this achieve?</p>\n", "opts": ["Parent and child never share any pages", "Copying of the address space is delayed until a page is written, speeding up process creation", "The child always runs exec() first", "All pages are copied immediately"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.46]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-6", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Mode bit", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>The hardware mode bit is ____ in user mode and ____ in kernel mode.</p>\n", "opts": ["0, 1", "1, 0", "1, 1", "0, 0"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.28]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-7", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Protection rings", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>On Intel processors with four protection rings:</p>\n", "opts": ["Ring 3 is kernel mode and ring 0 is user mode", "Ring 0 is kernel mode and ring 3 is user mode", "All four rings are heavily used", "Ring 1 is for the VMM only"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.29]</span>；rings 1、2 rarely used。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-8", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Trap", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A segmentation fault (protection violation) causes which type of mode transfer?</p>\n", "opts": ["System call", "Interrupt", "Trap or exception", "Context switch only"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：trap/exception = <strong>internal synchronous event</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[3.31]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-9", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Bounded buffer", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>The shared-memory bounded-buffer solution with <code>in</code> and <code>out</code> and no counter can hold at most:</p>\n", "opts": ["BUFFER_SIZE items", "BUFFER_SIZE − 1 items", "BUFFER_SIZE + 1 items", "Unlimited items"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.54]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-10", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Direct communication", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which is a property of direct communication in message passing?</p>\n", "opts": ["Messages go through mailboxes", "A link is associated with exactly one pair of processes", "A link may be associated with more than two processes", "It provides better modularity than indirect communication"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.59]</span>；缺點 = limited modularity。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-11", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Zero capacity", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>With a zero-capacity message queue:</p>\n", "opts": ["The sender never waits", "The sender waits only if the queue is full", "The sender must wait for the receiver (rendezvous)", "Messages are lost"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.64]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-12", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "UNIX FIFO", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about named pipes (FIFOs) in UNIX is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["They support full-duplex transmission over networks", "They are created with mkfifo(), appear as files, support half-duplex, and processes must be on the same machine", "They disappear when the creating process exits", "They require a parent-child relationship"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.69]</span>；Windows named pipes 先係 full-duplex、可跨機。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-13", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Ports", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about client–server sockets is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["Servers initiate the connection to clients", "All ports below 1024 are well known; clients pick a port above 1024", "HTTP uses port 22", "A socket is identified by the MAC address only"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.71]</span>；HTTP 80、SSH 22、FTP 21。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-14", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Orphan", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>When a parent terminates without calling wait(), its child process:</p>\n", "opts": ["Is immediately deleted by the kernel in all OSes", "Becomes an orphan and is re-parented to init/systemd, which periodically calls wait()", "Becomes a zombie forever", "Takes over the parent's PID"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[3.50]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-15", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "exec", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which is true about a successful exec() call?</p>\n", "opts": ["It returns the PID of the new program", "It returns 0 to the child", "It does not return; the process image is replaced", "It creates a new process"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：exec <strong>唔會建立新 process</strong>，只係 replace 現有 process 嘅 image <span class=\"sref\">[3.41]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-16", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "fork count", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>How many processes are there in total after: <code>fork(); fork() &amp;&amp; fork(); fork();</code></p>\n", "opts": ["8", "10", "12", "16"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：2 × 3 × 2 = <strong>12</strong>（<code>fork() &amp;&amp; fork()</code> 令每個 process 變 3 個）。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-17", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Interrupt vector", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>The interrupt vector is:</p>\n", "opts": ["A list of processes waiting for I/O", "A table of addresses of interrupt handlers, indexed by interrupt number", "The register that holds the next instruction address", "A queue of DMA requests"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：Ch3 summary。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch3-18", "ch": "ch3", "topic": "Nonmaskable interrupt", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A nonmaskable interrupt is reserved for events such as:</p>\n", "opts": ["Keyboard input", "Unrecoverable memory errors and power failure", "Timer expiry for RR", "Disk I/O completion"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：Ch3 summary；maskable 用於 device controllers。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-1", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Multicore challenges", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which is <strong>NOT</strong> one of the multicore programming challenges listed in the lecture?</p>\n", "opts": ["Dividing tasks", "Data dependency", "Testing and debugging", "Reducing the number of system calls"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：五大：dividing tasks、balance、data splitting、data dependency、testing &amp; debugging <span class=\"sref\">[4.9]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-2", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Windows TEB", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In Windows, which thread data structure lives in <strong>user space</strong> and contains the thread id, user-mode stack and thread-local storage?</p>\n", "opts": ["ETHREAD", "KTHREAD", "TEB", "PCB"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.36]</span>。ETHREAD、KTHREAD 喺 kernel space。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-3", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "clone()", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which call creates a Linux task that behaves like a thread?</p>\n", "opts": ["clone(SIGCHLD, 0)", "clone(CLONE_VM | CLONE_FS | CLONE_FILES | CLONE_SIGHAND, 0)", "fork() followed by exec()", "pthread_kill()"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：share address space、fs info、files、signal handlers <span class=\"sref\">[4.38]</span>；A = normal fork。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-4", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Linux threads", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>How does Linux treat threads?</p>\n", "opts": ["As lightweight processes with separate TCB and PCB structures", "As tasks — a thread is a process that shares certain resources with other tasks", "Only user-level threads are supported", "Through the many-to-one model"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.37]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-5", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Signal delivery", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A synchronous signal such as division by zero should be delivered to:</p>\n", "opts": ["Every thread in the process", "The thread that caused the signal", "A random thread", "The parent process"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.31]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-6", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Pthread cancellation default", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In Pthreads, the default cancellation type is:</p>\n", "opts": ["Asynchronous", "Deferred", "Disabled permanently", "Immediate"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.32]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-7", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Amdahl limit", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>An application is 50% parallel. As the number of cores approaches infinity, the maximum speedup is:</p>\n", "opts": ["1.5", "2", "4", "Infinite"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/0.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span></span></span> <strong>2</strong>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-8", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "One-to-one drawback", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>What is the main drawback of the one-to-one model?</p>\n", "opts": ["One blocking call blocks the whole process", "Threads cannot run in parallel", "Creating a user thread requires creating a kernel thread, so the number of threads may be restricted", "It is difficult to implement"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.23]</span>。A、B 係 many-to-one；D 係 many-to-many。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-9", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "Thread context switch", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Why is a context switch between two threads of the same process cheaper than between processes?</p>\n", "opts": ["Threads have no registers", "The address space stays the same", "Threads do not have stacks", "The OS does not save any state"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[4.14]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch4-10", "ch": "ch4", "topic": "fork in multithreaded process", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>If exec() is called immediately after fork() in a multithreaded process, which fork() version is appropriate?</p>\n", "opts": ["Duplicate all threads", "Duplicate only the calling thread", "Duplicate no threads", "It does not matter for correctness or efficiency"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：exec 會 replace 成個 process，複製所有 threads 係浪費 <span class=\"sref\">[4.28]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-1", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Dispatcher", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which is <strong>NOT</strong> a function of the dispatcher?</p>\n", "opts": ["Switching context", "Switching to user mode", "Jumping to the proper location in the user program", "Selecting the next process using the scheduling algorithm"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：揀 process 係 <strong>CPU scheduler</strong>；dispatcher 只負責交 CPU 畀佢 <span class=\"sref\">[5.7]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-2", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "RR waiting bound", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>With n processes and quantum q under RR (ignoring context switches), no process waits more than:</p>\n", "opts": ["nq", "(n − 1)q", "q / n", "n + q"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.11]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-3", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Quantum rule of thumb", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A common rule of thumb for choosing the RR quantum is:</p>\n", "opts": ["q should be smaller than the context-switch time", "80% of CPU bursts should be shorter than q", "q should equal the longest CPU burst", "q should be 1 ms"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.16]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-4", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Exponential averaging α = 0", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>With exponential averaging, if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> then:</p>\n", "opts": ["Only the last CPU burst counts", "Recent history does not count; the prediction never changes", "All bursts are weighted equally", "The prediction is always 0"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6389em;vertical-align:-0.2083em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2083em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1132em;\">τ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1132em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> <span class=\"sref\">[5.22]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-5", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "SJF as priority", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>SJF is a special case of priority scheduling where the priority is:</p>\n", "opts": ["The arrival time", "The inverse of the predicted next CPU burst", "The process ID", "The period of the task"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.25]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-6", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "MLFQ preemption rule", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In the lecture's MLFQ, when a job running from Q1 is preempted by a new arrival in Q0, it:</p>\n", "opts": ["Is demoted to Q2", "Joins the tail of Q1 with a fresh quantum", "Joins the head of Q1 with its remaining quantum", "Is moved to Q0"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.31]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-7", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Logical CPUs", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A quad-core processor with 2 hardware threads per core appears to the OS as how many logical processors?</p>\n", "opts": ["2", "4", "6", "8"], "ans": "D", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：4 × 2 = 8 <span class=\"sref\">[5.42]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-8", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Push migration", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Push migration means:</p>\n", "opts": ["An idle processor pulls a waiting task from a busy processor", "A specific task periodically checks loads and moves tasks from overloaded to idle/less-busy CPUs", "A process specifies the CPUs it may run on", "A thread is pinned to one core forever"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：A = pull migration <span class=\"sref\">[5.46]</span>；C = hard affinity <span class=\"sref\">[5.45]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-9", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Affinity system call", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In Linux, which system call supports hard affinity?</p>\n", "opts": ["sched_setaffinity()", "setpriority()", "clone()", "nice()"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.45]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-10", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "RM optimality", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Rate-monotonic scheduling is optimal in the sense that:</p>\n", "opts": ["It always achieves 100% CPU utilization", "If a task set cannot be scheduled by RM, it cannot be scheduled by any other static-priority algorithm", "It never misses deadlines", "It handles aperiodic tasks best"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.52]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-11", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "EDF requirement", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>What is the only requirement EDF places on a process?</p>\n", "opts": ["It must be periodic", "It must have a constant CPU burst", "It must announce its deadline to the scheduler when it becomes runnable", "Its period must be a power of 2"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.52]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-12", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "RM utilization", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Two periodic tasks: P1 (period 50, burst 25), P2 (period 80, burst 35). Under RM:</p>\n", "opts": ["Total utilization is 75% and no deadline is missed", "Total utilization ≈ 94% and P2 misses its deadline at 80 (finishes at 85)", "P1 misses its deadline", "EDF would also miss a deadline"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.50–5.51]</span>；EDF 可以全部 meet。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-13", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Deterministic modeling", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement about deterministic modeling is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["It uses probability distributions of CPU bursts", "It takes a predetermined workload and gives exact numbers, but results apply only to that workload", "It requires running the real system", "It is the most accurate method"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.54]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-14", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Response time (course definition)", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>RR with q = 4; P1 (24), P2 (3), P3 (3) all arrive at 0 in that order. Using the course definition, the average response time is:</p>\n", "opts": ["3.67", "5.67", "7", "15.67"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：end of first run − arrival = 4, 7, 10 → avg <strong>7</strong> <span class=\"sref\">[5.13]</span>。（3.67 係課本「first start」定義；5.67 係 avg WT；15.67 係 avg TAT）</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-15", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "Non-preemptive kernel / scheduling", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Scheduling that happens only when a process switches from running to waiting or terminates is called:</p>\n", "opts": ["Preemptive", "Non-preemptive (cooperative)", "Real-time", "Multilevel"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.6]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch5-16", "ch": "ch5", "topic": "SMP common queue issue", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>With a single common ready queue in SMP, what must the system guard against?</p>\n", "opts": ["Two processors choosing to schedule the same thread (race condition)", "Processor affinity being too strong", "Too many push migrations", "Memory stalls"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[5.39]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-1", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Disabling interrupts", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Why is disabling interrupts not a good critical-section solution on multiprocessors?</p>\n", "opts": ["It is not allowed in kernel mode", "It is inefficient — interrupts must be disabled on all processors", "It causes race conditions on uniprocessors", "It requires semaphores"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.13]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-2", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "CAS return value", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>compare_and_swap(&amp;value, expected, new_value) returns:</p>\n", "opts": ["new_value", "expected", "The original value of *value", "TRUE if the swap happened"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.17]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-3", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Negative semaphore", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In the blocking (no busy waiting) semaphore implementation, a value of −3 means:</p>\n", "opts": ["The semaphore is broken", "Three processes are waiting on the semaphore", "Three resources are available", "Three signals were lost"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.26]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-4", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Spinlock usage", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Spinlocks are most appropriate when:</p>\n", "opts": ["Locks are held for a long time on a uniprocessor", "Locks are held for short times on multiprocessor systems", "Processes must sleep while waiting", "Context switches are free"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.22]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-5", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Preemptive kernel", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Which statement is correct?</p>\n", "opts": ["A preemptive kernel is free from race conditions", "A non-preemptive kernel is essentially free from race conditions in kernel mode (on a single processor)", "Non-preemptive kernels are harder to make correct on SMP than preemptive ones", "Kernel code never has race conditions"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.12]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-6", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Kernel race example", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>The lecture's kernel race-condition example involves two processes calling fork() concurrently. Which variable is at risk?</p>\n", "opts": ["counter", "next_available_pid", "lock", "turn"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：same PID could be assigned to two processes <span class=\"sref\">[6.8]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-7", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "P and V", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In Dijkstra's notation, P() and V() correspond to:</p>\n", "opts": ["signal() and wait()", "wait() and signal()", "acquire() and test_and_set()", "lock() and fork()"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：P = proberen (test)，V = verhogen (increment) <span class=\"sref\">[6.24]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-8", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Semaphore deadlock", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>P0: wait(S); wait(Q); … P1: wait(Q); wait(S); … with S = Q = 1. What can happen?</p>\n", "opts": ["Starvation only", "Deadlock", "Race condition on S only", "Nothing; this is always safe"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.28]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-9", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Starvation in semaphore queue", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>Starvation (indefinite blocking) can occur with semaphores when:</p>\n", "opts": ["Processes are removed from the waiting queue in LIFO order", "The semaphore is initialized to 1", "signal() is atomic", "The waiting queue is FIFO"], "ans": "A", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.28]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-10", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Atomic increment", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>In <code>do { temp = *v; } while (temp != compare_and_swap(v, temp, temp + 1));</code>, why might the loop repeat?</p>\n", "opts": ["Because CAS always fails the first time", "Because another thread changed *v between reading temp and the CAS, so the CAS returned a different value", "Because temp + 1 overflows", "It never repeats"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：<span class=\"sref\">[6.21]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-11", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Counting semaphore initial value", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>A counting semaphore controlling access to 5 identical printers should be initialized to:</p>\n", "opts": ["0", "1", "5", "−5"], "ans": "C", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：initialized to the number of resources available <span class=\"sref\">[6.25]</span>。</p>\n"}, {"id": "P-ch6-12", "ch": "ch6", "topic": "Simple TAS lock", "kind": "new", "src": "P", "stem": "<p>The simple lock <code>while (test_and_set(&amp;lock)); /*CS*/ lock = false;</code> satisfies:</p>\n", "opts": ["Mutual exclusion and bounded waiting", "Mutual exclusion but not bounded waiting", "Bounded waiting but not mutual exclusion", "None of the requirements"], "ans": "B", "alt": null, "exp": "<p>解：要用 waiting[] 版本 <span class=\"sref\">[6.19]</span> 先有 bounded waiting。</p>\n"}];
